==Galician==

===Etymology===
From Old Galician and {{inh|gl|roa-opt|tomar}}, of {{unk|gl|title=unknown}} origin; perhaps from {{inh|gl|la|autumō|autumāre}}<ref>{{R:DCECH|tomar}}</ref> or from {{der|gl|gem|-}}.<ref>{{cite-book|author=T. C. Donkin|title=An Etymological Dictionary of the Romance Languages; chiefly from the German of F. Diez.|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=5uTYyRhLl0kC|accessdate=13 May 2018|year=1864|publisher=Williams and Norgate|page=431}}</ref> Cognate with {{cog|es|tomar}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/toˈmaɾ/|lang=gl}}

===Verb===
{{gl-verb|tom|ar}}

# {{lb|gl|transitive}} to [[take]]
#: {{syn|gl|coller}}
# {{lb|gl|transitive}} to [[grab]]
#: {{syn|gl|agarrar}}
# {{lb|gl|transitive}} to [[seize]], to [[capture]]
#: {{syn|gl|conquistar|prender}}
# {{lb|gl|transitive}} to [[drink]]
#: {{syn|gl|beber}}
# {{lb|gl|transitive}} to [[take]] (food, a pill, etc)
#: {{syn|gl|comer}}
# {{lb|gl|transitive}} to [[sunbathe]]
#: {{ux|gl|Ven acó '''tomar o sol'''.|Come here to '''sunbathe'''.}}
#: {{syn|gl|asollar}}
# {{indtr|gl|por}} to [[accept]], to [[receive]]
# {{inflection of|gl|tomar||1//3|s|futr|subj}}
# {{inflection of|gl|tomar||1//3|s|pr|inf}}

